{
  "_about": "Track themes (docs/DESIGN.md \u00a77.5). theme_art.py builds every texture listed here; the Godot side is game/configs/themes/<id>.tres. 'base' is the ground everywhere off the road, 'patch' the shapes painted on it (a sand trap, an ice pond); both name a fill in tools/comfy/pipeline.json ground and a surface in track.gd SURFACES. A theme with \"water\": true is a boat course (DESIGN.md \u00a720): 'road' names the deep-water channel's fill, the kerb colours are the channel's buoys, 'base' is the shallows. A theme with \"space\": true is a space course (DESIGN.md \u00a723): 'road' is the star lane's fill, the kerb colours are its beacon lights, 'base' is open space (dust) and 'patch' the clouds.",
